    description: "DEFERRED — gated on MEAS-1. The cheap first step before INC-1's full per-file generality: hypergumbo already knows workspace / package boundaries (supply-chain tiers / internal_package_roots / workspace siblings), so a PR touching only package A can re-analyze just A's subtree.\n\nCoarser than INC-1 (whole-package granularity, not per-file), but avoids INC-1's per-file purity-audit + complete-key hazards — a much lower-risk latency win when full-repo is too slow but per-file memoization is not yet justified.\n\nBlocked-by: MEAS-1. Relationship: a lighter alternative / precursor to INC-1; do whichever the MEAS-1 numbers justify."  # 3dd2
    fields: {}  # 3dd2
- op: discuss  # 3b46
  at: '2026-08-17T08:37:50Z'  # 3b46
  by: agent  # 3b46
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 3b46
  clock: 2  # 3b46
  nonce: 3b46  # 3b46
  message: "UNGATED. MEAS-1's decision rule now points HERE specifically. Detail and\ncaveats on WI-kazas; the short form:\n\n  small repo (67 py files)          33 s\n  medium (nats-server, 251 go)     119 s\n  large (whisper.cpp, 565 src)     201 s\n  MONOREPO (hypergumbo, 7 pkgs)    489 s\n\nWI-kazas's rule: \"minutes -> package-scoping (INC-2) earns its keep\". Three of\nthe four cells are minutes. The monorepo cell is 8.2 min — minutes, not the\n\"tens of minutes\" that would have pointed at per-file memoization (WI-madut)\ninstead. So this item is the one the numbers select, and WI-madut is still\ncorrectly deferred on the user-latency argument.\n\nTHE SECOND ARGUMENT, which is stronger than the band and which MEAS-1 did not\nmodel: this cost is paid PER EDIT in the local loop, not once. The results cache\nis keyed on a whole-tree state_hash, so every `pytest` invocation re-analyzes\nthe whole repo. Seven consecutive smart-test runs this session: 9m39s, 9m32s,\n8m49s, 9m05s, 9m08s, 9m17s, 8m30s — with 13-19 s of tests inside each. 18\nstate_hash cache dirs under this repo's fingerprint, mtimes matching those runs\none-to-one. Filed as WI-runiz.\n\nWHY THIS REPO IS THE IDEAL FIRST TARGET FOR PACKAGE SCOPING. hypergumbo is\nitself a 7-package workspace, and the overwhelming majority of its commits touch\nONE package's src tree. This session's own commits are typical: #389 and #390\neach touched only packages/hypergumbo-core/src. A package-scoped re-analysis\nwould have re-derived one package and reused six.\n\nWHAT TO CHECK BEFORE BUILDING IT, because the naive version is unsound here:\nsmart-test's consumer is a REVERSE slice, and a cross-package dependent must\nstill be found. Changing packages/hypergumbo-core/src has dependents in every\nlang package, so package-scoped ANALYSIS must be paired with a whole-graph\nRE-LINK over cached per-package results — the same \"irreducible remainder\" that\nWI-madut names for linkers. If the re-link is itself most of the 489 s, this\nbuys nothing, and that split (analysis vs linking share of the 489 s) is the\nnext measurement to take. It is cheap: the per-pass timers already exist in\nAnalysisRun.\n\nPriority P3 -> P2. Not P1: the analysis/link split above should be measured\nfirst, since it decides whether this item is worth building at all."  # 3b46
